    "author_association": "NONE",
    "body": "### Contributing guidelines\n\n- [X] I have read [CONTRIBUTING.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md)\n- [X] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\n- [X] I have updated 'mini.nvim' to latest version\n\n### Module(s)\n\nai\n\n### Description\n\nUsing *inside next Brace\"*(`inB`) textobject, the surrounding braces will be selected instead rather than the *next* nested braces.\r\n\r\n`this is an example {}` will be selected rather than `` (inside `{}`)\r\n\r\nomap says that this is caused by mini, but it may also be a fallback to a builtin textobject\r\n\r\n```\r\n:omap inB\r\n\r\no  in            <Lua 1089: ~/.local/share/nvim/lazy/mini.nvim/lua/mini/ai.lua:1120>\r\n                 Inside next textobject\r\no  i             <Lua 1082: ~/.local/share/nvim/lazy/mini.nvim/lua/mini/ai.lua:1120>\r\n                 Inside textobject\r\n\r\n```\r\n\r\n\n\n### Neovim version\n\nNVIM v0.10.0-dev-1696+g189e21ae5-Homebrew\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\n```\r\n{ this| is an example {} }\r\n```\r\n\r\n`|` being the cursor\r\n\r\n`vinB`\n\n### Expected behavior\n\nInside of `{}` is selected\n\n### Actual behavior\n\nInside of `{ this is an example {} }` is selected",
